WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.750
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:06.670
Most children in the West are brought up being
told that a jolly fat magic man delivers their

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:08.000
presents every year.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.150
But as we grow older and wiser we start to
think that that maybe isn’t the whole truth

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:19.000
and the disappearing mince pie and brandy
has a lot more to do with your actual father

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.410
than Father Christmas.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:26.410
But naysayers I’m here to present a different
point of view, and go with me on this one.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:29.920
What if Santa Claus, is real?

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.730
Well he could be.

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:36.300
And I’m not talking about magic but actual
science.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:41.740
What happens when we apply maths, formulas
and the laws of motion to a large man with

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:43.200
a brandy addiction?

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:48.610
But surely it’s impossible for one man to
deliver millions of presents to millions of

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.500
homes in just one night?

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.540
Not to mention the flying reindeer and sweat-shop
elves.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:01:00.300
Well depending on how naughty you’ve been
this year, you might be pleasantly surprised…

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:05.560
let’s take a look at the actual physics
behind Santa Claus and find out if we shouldn’t

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:09.640
be so quick to disbelieve in a very old Christmas
legend.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:14.610
So one of the major issues people have with
the big K. Kringle is that he couldn’t possibly

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:18.360
visit every house on Earth in one night.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.970
But the thing is he doesn’t have to.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:26.630
To start, he reportedly only visits children,
of which there are 2 billion of on Earth,

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:29.270
that’s people under the age of 18.

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:34.189
The average children per household across
the world is roughly 3.5.

00:01:34.189 --> 00:01:39.200
So that leaves 1 billion households for Santa
to visit on Christmas Eve.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:44.299
It’s commonly been accepted throughout history
that Santa doesn’t visit children of non-Christian

00:01:44.299 --> 00:01:48.939
religions such as Muslim, Jewish, Hindu and
Buddhist.

00:01:48.939 --> 00:01:54.659
So if we factor out those households that
leaves us with only 92 million homes for Santa

00:01:54.659 --> 00:01:57.920
to visit, that’s significantly less.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.470
Also Santa doesn’t have to fit all these
into just 24 hours on Christmas eve.

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:08.751
If he travels from East to West he would have
31 hours in which to deliver presents, thanks

00:02:08.751 --> 00:02:11.390
to timezone differences.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:16.672
This leaves Santa with roughly 1/1000th of
a second to get down the chimney, deliver

00:02:16.672 --> 00:02:20.510
presents and consume whatever treats have
been left out for him.

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:25.300
He would have to make 822 visits per second.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.130
A challenge indeed.

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:39.000
And that brings us to the ever so complicated
topic of flying reindeer.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:46.180
There are an estimated 300,000 species of
living organisms yet to be classified, and

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:50.780
there exists a bleedin snake that can fly,
so who are we to say there aren’t flying

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:53.800
reindeer somewhere out there.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:03:00.940
But one of the biggest obstacles stopping
Santa from being real is not magical deer

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:04.210
but the payload he would have to carry.

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:10.260
Even if every child only received a small
toy from Santa, around 800g on average, it

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:15.590
would result in a payload on Santa’s Sleigh
weighting 302 million kilograms.

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:21.100
And that’s not even counting all the coal
for all the horrible little terrors.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:27.340
Now consider that Santa would have to travel
at 650 miles per second to get around all

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:31.080
the required households in time for Christmas
morning.

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:39.959
302 million kilograms traveling at that speed
would exert a red-nose shattering 13.5 quintillion

00:03:39.959 --> 00:03:47.150
joules of energy on each reindeer, due to
the immense air pressure created at such speeds.

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:52.239
At those pressures Blitzen’s going to get
blitzed and Comet will turn into an actual

00:03:52.239 --> 00:03:53.269
comet.

00:03:53.269 --> 00:03:59.130
In short, Santa, his sleigh and his reindeer
would burst into a ball of flames and perish

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:02.510
instantaneously after setting off from the
North Pole.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:04.110
Soo yeah..

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.970
Merry Christmas!

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:11.530
But hold on kids, wipe away those tears, because
Thoughty2 backed up by some scientific papers

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:14.920
he read, is about to save Christmas.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:20.309
The strange science of Quantum mechanics allows
for some physics defying spectacles that seem

00:04:20.309 --> 00:04:24.270
to defy every scientific law you know.

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:29.879
And if we apply the laws of Quantum mechanics
to Santa Claus then it’s possible that he

00:04:29.879 --> 00:04:33.430
is a Macroscopic Quantum Object.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:38.319
This would allow him to be in multiple places
at once – meaning he could deliver presents

00:04:38.319 --> 00:04:41.090
to every child on Earth simultaneously.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:45.840
There’s also the added benefit that he can
keep and eye on Mrs. Claus whilst he’s away

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:46.960
for the night.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:51.449
Which is imperative after “Elf Gate” of
Christmas Eve 1984.

00:04:51.449 --> 00:04:57.460
Quantum mechanics is a branch of science that
studies the very, very small; subatomic particles.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:02.589
It is our current understanding that these
tiny particles, such as electrons can be in

00:05:02.589 --> 00:05:11.240
two or more places in the universe at the
exact same time, as long as nobody is watching.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:16.460
To prove this, scientists fired a single particle
into an opaque plate that had two slits in

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:17.460
it.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:21.770
The diffraction pattern on the other side
of the plate revealed that this singular particle

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:25.639
actually passed through both slits at the
same time.

00:05:25.639 --> 00:05:31.330
However, when detectors were setup to monitor
if the particle passed through each slit,

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:36.300
it only passed through one slit at a time,
but never both.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.289
Just because it was being watched.

00:05:38.289 --> 00:05:44.759
To put it as simply as possible, this happens
because the particle’s wavefunction collapses

00:05:44.759 --> 00:05:49.710
when it is being observed, so it can no longer
be in two places at once.

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:53.139
It’s similar to how Mrs. Claus can be in
a different place than she’s supposed to

00:05:53.139 --> 00:05:56.119
be, when Santa’s not watching.

00:05:56.119 --> 00:06:02.679
This explains why Santa Claus can never be
seen, because if he were his wavefunction

00:06:02.679 --> 00:06:04.180
would collapse.

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:09.149
So if this is true how come we know Santa
as a large jolly fellow and not an iddy-biddy

00:06:09.149 --> 00:06:11.050
little subatomic particle?

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:17.319
Well scientists have observed large clusters
of particles that seem to behave as one single

00:06:17.319 --> 00:06:23.139
particle, admittedly these clusters of particles
are nowhere near as large as our prospective

00:06:23.139 --> 00:06:27.539
Mr Claus, but have some imagination for goodness
sake.

00:06:27.539 --> 00:06:32.779
So if Santa and his reindeer are a cluster
of billions and billions of particles, acting

00:06:32.779 --> 00:06:39.740
together as one – he could theoretically
still adhere to the laws of quantum mechanics

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:45.809
and deliver lovely gifts to deserving children
all over the world, in just one night.

00:06:45.809 --> 00:06:50.849
This would also explain why his super secret
Bond-villain, death star base of toy-construction

00:06:50.849 --> 00:06:53.270
is tucked away in the North Pole.

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:59.120
Because quantum particles only behave in this
manner in very, very cold environments.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:07.709
Scientists have only observed the behavior
at close to absolute zero; minus 273 C, which

00:07:07.709 --> 00:07:10.470
is somewhat colder than the north pole.

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:20.059
But then, we have to allow for some magic
at Christmas, don’t we?

00:07:20.059 --> 00:07:28.439
Thanks for the view.

